WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.153
Kinda Cute, written QindaQt, is a free and open source Wayland desktop.

2
00:00:05.153 --> 00:00:10.305
You get a shell, settings, a file manager, native tools, and an

3
00:00:10.305 --> 00:00:15.458
optional office suite. This is a captured session, not a concept picture.

4
00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:20.611
The Welcome guide starts with the main idea: keep ordinary windows until

5
00:00:20.611 --> 00:00:24.217
you choose to make them work together.

6
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:27.508
Here are Files and Settings as separate, working windows.

7
00:00:27.508 --> 00:00:31.631
I hold Meta and Shift and drag Settings toward the left edge

8
00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:35.066
of Files. The preview tells me where it will land.

9
00:00:35.066 --> 00:00:38.845
Release, and they share one movable frame with a live split.

10
00:00:38.845 --> 00:00:42.624
I can drag the divider to give either app more room.

11
00:00:42.624 --> 00:00:46.403
Each member keeps working and still has its own title controls.

12
00:00:46.403 --> 00:00:50.181
The group menu handles detach, ungroup, and moving the whole group;

13
00:00:50.181 --> 00:00:54.217
closing the frame asks what to do with its members.

14
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:59.198
The same gesture has a second answer. Drop near the middle instead

15
00:00:59.198 --> 00:01:03.978
of an edge, and Files and Settings become pages in one container.

16
00:01:03.978 --> 00:01:08.361
I switch between those real applications in the shared tab row.

17
00:01:08.361 --> 00:01:13.142
A page can itself contain splits, so a container can hold a

18
00:01:13.142 --> 00:01:16.727
larger project without turning every window into a tile.

19
00:01:16.727 --> 00:01:21.508
Pull a member's own title strip into empty space to detach it.

20
00:01:21.508 --> 00:01:26.289
You can also open the group menu, or use Meta Shift D

21
00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:31.070
and choose a target with arrows, T for a tab, or D

22
00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.467
to detach.

23
00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:37.264
Settings is where the desktop shape changes. In Customize I choose Classic

24
00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:41.861
Taskbar, then restore Menu and Dock. Those are two of eleven starting

25
00:01:41.861 --> 00:01:46.458
layouts. A layout changes the panels and applets; it does not erase

26
00:01:46.458 --> 00:01:51.055
the color theme I chose. Right click a panel for Edit Panels,

27
00:01:51.055 --> 00:01:55.653
then move items, add or duplicate applets, and save the result as

28
00:01:55.653 --> 00:02:00.467
your own preset. Your starting point is only a starting point.

29
00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:05.660
Appearance previews the real window chrome around ordinary application controls.

30
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:11.652
I browse the theme cards and select Graphite. The draft preview changes

31
00:02:11.652 --> 00:02:17.644
before I apply it. A theme brings its palette, window and container

32
00:02:17.644 --> 00:02:23.636
decoration, title buttons, and button arrangement together. Fine tune this theme opens

33
00:02:23.636 --> 00:02:29.629
the details: button style and side, title height, corner shape, and container

34
00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:35.621
controls. Wallpaper and fonts have their own tabs. Apply commits the draft;

35
00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:39.217
Revert returns to the saved look.

36
00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:44.270
Here is QindaQt's own arrangement: a thin top ledger, a smart shelf

37
00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:48.314
on the left, and compact instruments at the bottom right.

38
00:02:48.314 --> 00:02:53.168
The dark theme and Compiler Club wallpaper give it a distinct home,

39
00:02:53.168 --> 00:02:58.217
while the same ordinary File Manager moves freely across the desktop.

40
00:02:58.417 --> 00:03:04.061
Classic Taskbar puts launching, running windows, and status on one familiar bar.

41
00:03:04.061 --> 00:03:09.704
Its paired Classic Blue theme and the Qinda Bliss hills make the

42
00:03:09.704 --> 00:03:15.348
Windows-style starting point immediately recognizable. This is a live session, and its

43
00:03:15.348 --> 00:03:18.300
panels can still be edited.

44
00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:22.183
Centered Taskbar moves the launch cluster to the middle.

45
00:03:22.183 --> 00:03:27.093
Daylight supplies the light controls and title bar, and Porcelain Dawn carries

46
00:03:27.093 --> 00:03:32.003
that calm through the wallpaper. Pick it if you want a modern

47
00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:35.467
taskbar without giving up QindaQt's window containers.

48
00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:40.926
Corner Bar takes a BeOS-like route: a compact panel in the corner

49
00:03:40.926 --> 00:03:45.747
and a short title tab instead of a full colored strip.

50
00:03:45.747 --> 00:03:51.006
Marigold gives it amber controls. Sea Glass and Lilac offer other colors

51
00:03:51.006 --> 00:03:55.550
and corner radii; the layout itself remains the same.

52
00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:00.610
Workspace Dock sets a column down the right side, inspired by NeXT.

53
00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:05.064
Graphite gives its windows a darker, quieter treatment against Ink Tide.

54
00:04:05.064 --> 00:04:09.924
Open applications keep their own real windows; the dock is the route

55
00:04:09.924 --> 00:04:15.383
into a workspace, not a rule about how you must arrange it.

56
00:04:15.583 --> 00:04:21.752
Program Groups recalls the Windows three point one idea of organized application

57
00:04:21.752 --> 00:04:27.920
groups, with a top bar and windows that can minimize to desktop

58
00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:34.088
icons. Classic Grey supplies the matching squared decoration. Familiar history becomes another

59
00:04:34.088 --> 00:04:38.800
editable profile rather than a separate operating system.

60
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.455
Menu and Dock is the shipped default. The application menu sits across

61
00:04:43.455 --> 00:04:47.911
the top, while the dock lives below with File Manager near the

62
00:04:47.911 --> 00:04:52.366
beginning and Trash at the end. Its Mist theme and Jade Fold

63
00:04:52.366 --> 00:04:57.050
wallpaper keep the menu, dock, and windows in one visual family.

64
00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:02.072
Overview starts from workspaces and an Activities entry along the top.

65
00:05:02.072 --> 00:05:06.455
The darker Slate theme is paired here with Ink Tide.

66
00:05:06.455 --> 00:05:10.400
It is a different path through the same desktop:

67
00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:15.383
QindaQt's apps, settings, and optional window grouping are still there.

68
00:05:15.583 --> 00:05:19.948
Command Rail puts launch and switching controls down the left and a

69
00:05:19.948 --> 00:05:24.312
search HUD at the top. Dusk and Qinda Punk make that vertical

70
00:05:24.312 --> 00:05:28.677
layout feel deliberate. If you like a side launcher, begin here and

71
00:05:28.677 --> 00:05:32.550
then rearrange the rail to suit your own applications.

72
00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:37.418
Compact Flexible gives you a lean top panel and a smaller launcher

73
00:05:37.418 --> 00:05:42.086
below. The light theme and Porcelain Dawn backdrop make the window edges

74
00:05:42.086 --> 00:05:46.755
easy to read. It leaves room for the task at hand and

75
00:05:46.755 --> 00:05:50.467
plenty of room to change the panels later.

76
00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:54.491
Minimal strips the shell down so the application takes the stage.

77
00:05:54.491 --> 00:05:58.316
Ink Tide and the dark glass theme keep the frame quiet.

78
00:05:58.316 --> 00:06:02.488
You can bring back any panel or applet when you need it;

79
00:06:02.488 --> 00:06:06.217
choosing a sparse profile is not a permanent commitment.

80
00:06:06.417 --> 00:06:12.169
File Manager is a native app, not just a screenshot of a

81
00:06:12.169 --> 00:06:17.922
folder. Browse files, switch views, use bookmarks, and open the wallpaper collection

82
00:06:17.922 --> 00:06:23.674
shown here. QindaQt also includes Settings, Text Editor, Terminal, a viewer for

83
00:06:23.674 --> 00:06:27.989
images and PDFs, QindaMPV for media, and System Monitor.

84
00:06:27.989 --> 00:06:33.741
They use the desktop's visual language instead of looking like visitors from

85
00:06:33.741 --> 00:06:35.300
another system.

86
00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:40.631
Audio is more than a volume slider. Audio One has five physical

87
00:06:40.631 --> 00:06:45.761
and three virtual input strips, five hardware buses and three virtual buses.

88
00:06:45.761 --> 00:06:50.892
You can set each send independently, watch live meters, use processing racks,

89
00:06:50.892 --> 00:06:54.740
record, and configure manual stereo streams to another computer.

90
00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:59.870
In this captured example a test tone enters Virtual Input, I enable

91
00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:05.001
its B one send, and the B one meter responds in an

92
00:07:05.001 --> 00:07:06.883
isolated PipeWire graph.

93
00:07:07.083 --> 00:07:12.503
The companion Office suite handles real work too. This budget is an

94
00:07:12.503 --> 00:07:16.568
editable workbook for Signal Garden, a sample neighborhood event.

95
00:07:16.568 --> 00:07:21.988
I double the lighting quantity and the formula raises cost above the

96
00:07:21.988 --> 00:07:26.957
project's ceiling. Then I return it to one before the pitch.

97
00:07:26.957 --> 00:07:32.377
The related brief, chart, slide deck, and field notes open in QindaWrite,

98
00:07:32.377 --> 00:07:37.797
QindaCalc, QindaShow, and QindaNote. You can download the same files from the

99
00:07:37.797 --> 00:07:39.300
Office site.
